<title>USA: ComEd Dresden Ill. nuke resumes full power.</title>
<headline>ComEd Dresden Ill. nuke resumes full power.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Edison Co's Dresden 2 nuclear unit has resumed full power output at its 794 megawatt rated capacity, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Monday.</p>
<p>The unit, in Morris, Illinois, has been ramping up output since late last week, and was expected to hit full power by Saturday.</p>
<p>It shut Monday a week ago when feedwater levels fell below acceptable levels.</p>
<p>ComEd is a subsidiary of Unicom Corp.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk + 212 859 1621))</p>
</text>
